course: dictionary
lesson: 1756
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and claw is one of them. Claw can be a thing (a noun) or an action (a verb). The words around it tell you which meaning fits, so read the whole sentence before you decide.
explain: «The cat's sharp claws dug into the sofa.» Here claw is a thing: the sharp nail on the end of a paw. Now read «The cat clawed at the sofa.» Clawed is an action: the cat was scratching or tearing with its claws. Ask yourself, is this a thing or something being done?
explain: «The crab grabbed the shell with its big claw.» The clue is grabbed. A crab's claw is its pincer, and it uses it to hold things. Try the meaning in the sentence: "the crab grabbed the shell with its big sharp nail" does not quite fit, so the pincer meaning is the better choice.
fact: A claw is a sharp, curved nail on the foot of an animal or bird, like a cat's, eagle's or bear's.
fact: The claw of a crab, lobster or scorpion is called a pincer, and it is used to grab things.
fact: To claw means to scratch, tear or grab with claws or fingernails.
fact: «Claw back» means to get something back with great effort.
fact: Cats can pull their claws in, but dogs cannot, so a cat's claws stay sharp and safe until it needs them.
exercise: «The eagle's claws gripped the branch tightly.» What is a claw here? | A loud cry from the sky | *A sharp curved nail on a bird's foot | A branch that has broken off | A feather on its wing
exercise: «The lobster snapped its claw shut.» What is the claw in this sentence? | A bird's wing | A sharp tooth | A small bell | *The pincer a lobster uses to grab things
exercise: «The cat clawed at the door to be let in.» What does clawed mean? | Sang loudly | *Scratched or tore with its claws | Ate its dinner quickly | Slept soundly
test: «It took her a week to claw back the money she had lost.» What does claw back mean? | Count it quickly | Give it away to a friend | Lose it all again | *Get it back with great effort
test: «A claw hammer has a split end for pulling out nails.» Does claw mean an animal's nail here? | *No, it is the name of a tool, not an animal part | Yes, it is a sharp nail on a foot | Yes, it is a crab's pincer | No, it means to scratch
exam: «He had to claw his way up the muddy cliff, grabbing roots and rocks.» What does claw his way mean? | Walked slowly along a flat path | Waited at the bottom for help | Flew quickly over the top | *Moved upwards with great effort
